 Credentials/port are synthetic examples; use only a dedicated owned fixture. Install dependencies independently. Replace pg or scoped policy predicates while preserving all source/current-authority/audit/transaction/failure/clock contracts. No actual policy content/evaluator/finding is seeded in Root. O09/O11/staffed operating approval, actual rank assessment/reassessment/projections/APIUI and independent/UAT/business/release acceptance remain separate. See [module contracts](../../docs/raid-practice-trial-ownership.md) for API/events/errors/migration/recovery and [task evidence](../../planning/task-evidence/T013-trial-ownership/) for actual results.
+
+The example now also consumes the portable [ownership HTTP contract](../../docs/raid-practice-ownership-http.md) through Web Request/Response GET/HEAD/POST. Synthetic server-owned identity/origin configuration composes real transactions; no public listener is exposed and real hosts must supply quotas/auth/origin. The test records and corrects findings, checks current/history and stale CAS, rejects changed retry bodies, replays the original command after withdrawal/writeoff, and denies foreign/wrong-purpose/revoked scope without notes. The canonical HTTP source and bounded JSON dependency are explicitly linked and copied for independent installation. Root adapters/routes remain separate; the action UI and full assessment acceptance remain unverified.
+
+The [ownership form](../../docs/raid-practice-ownership-ui.md) extends this own-installed host with explicit React/ReactDOM/types and canonical context/client/pure-schema/component links. It observes actual original case + approved policy + current finding in one committed transaction, then server-renders the real editor and original evidence. Existing HTTP save/correction/retry/history tests remain actual PostgreSQL. No Next or Root auth is required. Pending private command recovery in the editor lasts only for the mounted controller, with no browser persistence; durable cross-device drafts remain unsupported.
